  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.0.4: A publish no longer leaks a RabbitMQ channel per outbox message, which used to exhaust the connection until every publish failed. A delay queue is named per exchange, delay and routing key, so a second event type sharing a delay no longer fails its declare and dead-letter silently. The consumer and core-exchange hosted services wait for a broker that is not up yet, with backoff, instead of terminating the process. The outbox is read oldest first.",
